    <string name="description_songo">A game of patience and strategy. Sow seeds and capture more than your opponent.</string>
    <string name="description_pirogue">Race a dugout canoe on the river. Steer around logs: each collision slows you down.</string>
    <string name="description_dochi">Dodge the balls thrown from both sides. Survive until the timer runs out to win.</string>
    <string name="description_quiz">Ten questions about Cameroon’s regions, food, music and landmarks.</string>
    <string name="rules_songo">Each side has five pits with five seeds. Tap one of your pits to sow its seeds one by one: up your column, then down the other one. If your last seed lands in an opposing pit that now holds 2 or 3 seeds, you capture them, plus the opposing pits just before it that also hold 2 or 3. You may not capture every seed on the other side, and you must feed an empty side when you can. More than 25 captured seeds wins. The round also ends when no move is possible, a position repeats three times, or after 200 turns; each side then keeps its own seeds.</string>
    <string name="rules_pirogue">Both canoes paddle by themselves at the same speed and race on the same river. Hold the arrow buttons to steer around the floating logs. Each log you hit slows you down for a moment. The first canoe across the line wins.</string>
    <string name="rules_dochi">Two throwers aim balls at you from the left and the right. Move with the joystick and stay alive until the timer ends: 30 seconds on level 1, 40 on level 2 and 45 on level 3. The longer you survive, the higher your score.</string>
    <string name="rules_quiz">Answer ten questions. Each correct answer earns 50 points and 10 XP. Get at least 6 right to win the round.</string>

